1
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,330
Man, this is weird.

2
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:09,210
Ever realize Cap'n Crunch's eyebrows are on his hat?

3
00:00:09,460 --> 00:00:10,550
That's what's weird?

4
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,720
The man's been captain of a cereal for 40 years.

5
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:17,760
Whoa, yuck!

6
00:00:17,930 --> 00:00:18,970
What?

7
00:00:19,260 --> 00:00:21,890
The spoon! You licked and you put.

8
00:00:24,350 --> 00:00:26,270
You licked and you put.

9
00:00:26,480 --> 00:00:27,560
Yeah, so?

10
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:32,530
Don't you see how gross that is? It's like you using my toothbrush!

11
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,740
You used my toothbrush?

12
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:40,240
Only because I used the red one to unclog the drain.

13
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:42,580
Mine is the red one!

14
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:48,580
Oh, God! Can open. Worms everywhere!

15
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:51,920
Why can't we use the same toothbrush...

16
00:00:52,130 --> 00:00:54,090
but we can use the same soap?

17
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:58,140
Because soap is soap. It's self-cleaning.

18
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,720
The next time you shower...

19
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:04,850
think about the last thing I wash and the first thing you wash.

20
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:16,730
∮ So no one told you life was gonna be this way ∮

21
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:21,440
∮ Your job's a joke, you're broke, your love life's D.O.A. ∮

22
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:26,160
∮ It's like you're always stuck in second gear ∮

23
00:01:26,620 --> 00:01:28,720
∮ When it hasn't been your day, ∮

24
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:31,720
∮ your week, your month, or even your year ∮

25
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:35,680
∮ but I'll be there for you ∮

26
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:37,510
∮ When the rain starts to pour ∮

27
00:01:37,510 --> 00:01:40,630
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

28
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:42,470
∮ Like I've been there before ∮

29
00:01:42,470 --> 00:01:45,480
∮ I'll be there for you ∮

30
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:49,140
∮ 'Cause you're there for me too ∮

31
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:56,400
- Hey.     - Hey.

32
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:59,530
Look at you fancy lads!

33
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,200
What's the occasion?

34
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:04,120
You know that guy on my show that's in a coma?

35
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:07,040
He's having a brunch.

36
00:02:08,290 --> 00:02:09,750
Ready when you are.

37
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,540
I can't believe you're actually getting tattoos.

38
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,840
You guys are getting tattoos?

39
00:02:16,050 --> 00:02:19,380
But you cannot tell Ross because I wanna surprise him.

40
00:02:19,630 --> 00:02:22,430
Wow, this is wild! What are you gonna get?

41
00:02:22,680 --> 00:02:24,970
I'm getting a lily.

42
00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:28,520
For my mom, because her name's Lily.

43
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:32,900
That's lucky. What if her name was Big Ugly Splotch?

44
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:36,780
- Where you getting it?     - On my shoulder.

45
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:38,030
What?

46
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:40,200
What's on your shoulder?

47
00:02:40,530 --> 00:02:41,660
A chip.

48
00:02:44,410 --> 00:02:47,290
- A tattoo. I'm getting a tattoo.     - A tattoo?

49
00:02:47,540 --> 00:02:49,370
Why? Why would you wanna do that?

50
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,170
- Hi.     - Hi.

51
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:53,540
You don't think they're kind of cool?

52
00:02:53,790 --> 00:02:55,670
No. Sorry, I don't.

53
00:02:55,880 --> 00:02:59,170
Why would anyone pay someone to scar their body for life?

54
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,510
What if it doesn't come out right?

55
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:04,800
It's like having a bad haircut all the time.

56
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,770
Why is everyone staring at me?

57
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:11,730
Sign this card for Dad. Richard will be here soon.

58
00:03:11,940 --> 00:03:13,770
Richard's going to the party too?

59
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:16,360
He's my parents' best friend. He has to go.

60
00:03:16,610 --> 00:03:19,860
So is today the day you'll tell them about you two?

61
00:03:20,110 --> 00:03:24,200
Yeah, for my dad's birthday, I decided to give him a stroke.

62
00:03:25,070 --> 00:03:27,330
No, I think you should tell them.

63
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:31,000
I don't know how serious he is. Until I do, I won't say anything.

64
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:33,580
I don't think Mom and Dad would mind.

65
00:03:33,790 --> 00:03:36,790
Remember when you were 9 and Richard was 30, Dad said:

66
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,840
"God, I hope they get together."

67
00:03:44,050 --> 00:03:45,140
Shall we?

68
00:03:45,390 --> 00:03:46,930
Okay, wait.

69
00:03:47,430 --> 00:03:48,810
You know what?

70
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:52,140
Ross, let's switch places. You get in the middle.

71
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:55,810
This looks like we're trying to cover something up.

72
00:03:56,020 --> 00:03:59,650
You could come in straddling him, they still wouldn't believe it.

73
00:04:02,240 --> 00:04:03,400
We're here!

74
00:04:03,740 --> 00:04:06,370
- Hi, kids!     - The children!

75
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:09,450
- Happy birthday, Dad.     - Thank you.

76
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:10,910
Happy birthday!

77
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,620
So you kids thanked Dr. Burke for the ride?

78
00:04:13,870 --> 00:04:17,790
Actually, Mom, I think Monica thanked him for the both of us.

79
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:21,550
So you kids take the train in?

80
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:24,260
No, Richard Burke gave them a ride.

81
00:04:24,470 --> 00:04:25,760
Speaking of whom...

82
00:04:26,010 --> 00:04:29,890
I hear he's got some 20-year-old twinkie in the city.

83
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:35,770
Finger cramp! Oh, God!

84
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:38,360
Sorry. Here, let me get that, Mom.

85
00:04:40,360 --> 00:04:43,440
So Richard's shopping in the junior section?

86
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:45,780
Are we still on that?

87
00:04:46,030 --> 00:04:49,490
You just know she's got the IQ of a napkin.

88
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,580
She's probably not even pretty.

89
00:04:51,830 --> 00:04:55,540
Just young enough so that everything is still pointing up.

90
00:05:03,630 --> 00:05:04,970
Can you believe this place?

91
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:07,050
I know. This is a great apartment.

92
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:10,180
In the bathroom there's mirrors on both sides of you.

93
00:05:10,430 --> 00:05:13,770
When you're in there, it's like peeing with the Rockettes.

94
00:05:14,310 --> 00:05:16,600
Well, there's my fantasy come true.

95
00:05:17,190 --> 00:05:18,230
Seriously.

96
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:20,480
Hey.

97
00:05:20,650 --> 00:05:22,650
We were just saying, great apartment!

98
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:24,820
Thanks. You want it?

99
00:05:25,070 --> 00:05:26,530
I'm moving to a bigger place.

100
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,490
You should take this one.

101
00:05:29,120 --> 00:05:30,910
Can you see me in a place like this?

102
00:05:31,490 --> 00:05:34,580
Why not? You hate park views and high ceilings?

103
00:05:34,830 --> 00:05:36,830
Come on, I'll show you the kitchen.

104
00:05:38,540 --> 00:05:41,040
That's all right, I saw a kitchen this morning.

105
00:05:41,210 --> 00:05:42,290
On TV.

106
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:44,960
Stop talking. Okay!

107
00:05:46,170 --> 00:05:48,720
- Come on, tell us!     - Is she really 20?

108
00:05:48,930 --> 00:05:50,800
I am not telling you guys anything.

109
00:05:51,050 --> 00:05:53,850
Come on, it's my birthday. Let me live vicariously!

110
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,730
Dad, you really don't want to do that.

111
00:05:56,930 --> 00:05:59,600
What's a little midlife crisis between friends?

112
00:05:59,850 --> 00:06:01,310
Would you let it go?

113
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:04,980
I know what you're going through. When I turned 50, I got the Porsche.

114
00:06:05,190 --> 00:06:07,490
You got your own little speedster.

115
00:06:08,280 --> 00:06:11,160
- Seriously, it's not like that.     - Tell you what.

116
00:06:11,410 --> 00:06:15,370
Maybe one of these weekends you can borrow the car and I could...

117
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:18,000
Dad, I beg you not to finish that sentence!

118
00:06:18,370 --> 00:06:20,040
What? I'm kidding!

119
00:06:20,330 --> 00:06:23,130
You know I'd never let him touch the Porsche.

120
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:32,090
Okay, Rach.

121
00:06:33,010 --> 00:06:35,470
Which lily? This lily or that lily?

122
00:06:36,100 --> 00:06:38,390
- Well, I...     - I like this lily.

123
00:06:38,640 --> 00:06:41,060
It's more open and that's like my mom.

124
00:06:41,310 --> 00:06:43,770
She had a more open, giving spirit.

125
00:06:44,270 --> 00:06:46,270
Foghorn Leghorn!

126
00:06:48,030 --> 00:06:50,240
Blond girl? You're in room two.

127
00:06:50,450 --> 00:06:52,950
Not-so-blond girl, you're with me.

128
00:06:53,660 --> 00:06:55,240
- Here we go!     - Uh-huh.

129
00:06:56,290 --> 00:06:57,740
You're not going.

130
00:06:57,950 --> 00:06:59,000
Uh-huh.

131
00:06:59,160 --> 00:07:01,210
Is this because of what Ross said?

132
00:07:01,580 --> 00:07:02,670
No.

133
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:06,590
- Well, yeah, maybe.     - I don't believe this.

134
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:10,670
Is this how this relationship works? Ross equals boss?

135
00:07:11,840 --> 00:07:14,050
Come on, what is this, 1922?

136
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:16,010
What's 1922?

137
00:07:16,810 --> 00:07:18,770
Just, you know, a long time ago.

138
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:23,810
When men used to tell women what to do a lot.

139
00:07:24,150 --> 00:07:27,690
Then there was suffrage, which was a good thing. But it sounds horrible.

140
00:07:31,150 --> 00:07:32,530
Do you want this tattoo?

141
00:07:32,780 --> 00:07:34,780
Yes, I do. It's just that Ross...

142
00:07:35,870 --> 00:07:37,780
Is your boyfriend the boss of you?

143
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:40,750
No.

144
00:07:41,040 --> 00:07:42,580
Who is the boss of you?

145
00:07:44,130 --> 00:07:45,290
You?

146
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,880
No. You are the boss of you!

147
00:07:49,130 --> 00:07:52,050
You march in there and get that tattoo on your hip!

148
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:54,050
Go!

149
00:08:00,180 --> 00:08:01,390
How you doing?

150
00:08:01,600 --> 00:08:03,230
I'm a twinkie!

151
00:08:04,310 --> 00:08:06,560
Really? I'm a hero.

152
00:08:09,320 --> 00:08:10,980
This is so hard.

153
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:14,280
Yeah, I know. I hate it too.

154
00:08:14,570 --> 00:08:17,240
Look, maybe we should just tell them.

155
00:08:17,490 --> 00:08:20,120
Maybe we should just tell your parents first.

156
00:08:20,700 --> 00:08:22,410
My parents are dead.

157
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:25,750
God, you are so lucky!

158
00:08:27,500 --> 00:08:29,500
I mean... Well, you know what I mean.

159
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:32,420
Just hang in there, okay?

160
00:08:33,130 --> 00:08:35,760
Okay, I'll go out first, all right?

161
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:44,480
Judy! Going to the bathroom. Good for you!

162
00:08:47,690 --> 00:08:51,400
Thank you, Richard. I appreciate the support.

163
00:08:55,530 --> 00:08:56,610
Honey.

164
00:08:57,410 --> 00:09:00,410
Seen my Harmon Killebrew bat? Bob doesn't believe I have one.

165
00:09:00,660 --> 00:09:02,120
I have no idea.

166
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:05,120
Did you know Richard has a twinkie in the city?

167
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:10,380
I know. He's a new man. It's like a scene from Cocoon.

168
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:14,510
I just never would have pictured Richard with a bimbo.

169
00:09:14,760 --> 00:09:17,630
He told Johnny Shapiro that she's quite a girl.

170
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:21,430
He told Johnny that he thinks he's falling in love with her.

171
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:24,140
- Really?     - I've never seen him this happy.

172
00:09:24,390 --> 00:09:25,810
So, Jack...

173
00:09:26,270 --> 00:09:28,900
ever think about trading me in for a younger model?

174
00:09:29,150 --> 00:09:31,270
Of course not.

175
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:34,030
With you, it's like I've got two 25-year-olds.

176
00:09:38,610 --> 00:09:40,240
Oh, Jack, stop!

177
00:09:40,450 --> 00:09:42,280
Come on!

178
00:09:42,990 --> 00:09:45,410
It's my birthday!

179
00:09:49,670 --> 00:09:50,830
Can we drop this?

180
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:53,300
I am not interested in the guy's apartment.

181
00:09:53,590 --> 00:09:57,720
Oh, please. I saw the way you were checking out his moldings.

182
00:09:57,970 --> 00:09:59,010
You want it.

183
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:01,260
Why would I want another apartment?

184
00:10:01,510 --> 00:10:03,680
I've already got an apartment that I love.

185
00:10:03,930 --> 00:10:06,060
It wouldn't kill you to say it once in a while.

186
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:13,770
All right. You want the truth? I'm thinking about it.

187
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:16,480
- What?     - I'm sorry.

188
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:19,610
I'm 28. I've never lived alone...

189
00:10:19,820 --> 00:10:22,780
and I'm at a place where I got enough money...

190
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:24,530
that I don't need a roommate.

191
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:28,000
Whoa, whoa, whoa. I don't need a roommate either.

192
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:30,750
I can afford to live here by myself.

193
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,630
I may have to bring in somebody once a week to lick the silverware.

194
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:37,960
Why are you getting so bent out of shape?

195
00:10:38,170 --> 00:10:40,470
We didn't agree to live together forever.

196
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:42,340
We're not Bert and Ernie.

197
00:10:44,470 --> 00:10:45,560
You know what?

198
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:47,560
If this is the way you feel...

199
00:10:47,810 --> 00:10:49,640
then maybe you should take it.

200
00:10:50,560 --> 00:10:52,690
- That's how I feel.     - Then maybe you should take it!

201
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:53,900
Maybe I will!

202
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:55,400
- Fine with me!     - Great!

203
00:10:55,650 --> 00:10:58,400
You can spend more quality time with your real friends...

204
00:10:58,610 --> 00:11:00,280
the spoons!

205
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:03,410
Whose drink can I freshen?

206
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,950
Almost time for cake!

207
00:11:16,170 --> 00:11:17,380
Mon?

208
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:19,300
Mon, are you okay?

209
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:23,550
- Remember that video of Mom and Dad?     - Yeah?

210
00:11:24,010 --> 00:11:26,350
- Well, I just caught the live show.     - Ew!

211
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:40,400
- Hey there.     - What?

212
00:11:41,070 --> 00:11:45,030
Nothing. I just heard something nice about you.

213
00:11:46,030 --> 00:11:47,120
Really?

214
00:11:47,410 --> 00:11:48,700
Richard?

215
00:11:50,290 --> 00:11:53,750
- Your son isn't seeing anyone, is he?     - Not that I know of.

216
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:57,460
I was thinking, why doesn't he give Monica a call?

217
00:12:01,130 --> 00:12:02,920
That's an idea.

218
00:12:03,130 --> 00:12:06,260
Well, actually, I'm already seeing someone.

219
00:12:06,470 --> 00:12:07,720
Oh?

220
00:12:08,310 --> 00:12:09,600
Oh...

221
00:12:11,770 --> 00:12:13,600
She never tells us anything.

222
00:12:13,850 --> 00:12:16,270
Ross, did you know Monica's seeing someone?

223
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:19,820
Mom, there are so many people in my life.

224
00:12:20,400 --> 00:12:23,070
Some are seeing people and some aren't.

225
00:12:23,320 --> 00:12:25,030
Is that crystal?

226
00:12:27,740 --> 00:12:29,580
So who's the mystery man?

227
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:32,620
Well, he's a doctor.

228
00:12:32,870 --> 00:12:34,290
A real doctor?

229
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:36,710
No, a doctor of meat.

230
00:12:37,420 --> 00:12:39,420
Of course he's a real doctor.

231
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:41,300
And he's handsome.

232
00:12:42,210 --> 00:12:44,970
And he's sweet, and I know you'd like him.

233
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:47,180
Well, that's wonderful.

234
00:12:53,230 --> 00:12:55,270
Mom, it's okay.

235
00:12:55,440 --> 00:12:56,520
It is, Judy.

236
00:12:56,730 --> 00:12:58,190
Jack!

237
00:13:00,110 --> 00:13:02,780
Could you come in here for a moment?

238
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:04,320
Now!

239
00:13:05,150 --> 00:13:07,780
- Found it!     - I'll take that, Dad.

240
00:13:11,450 --> 00:13:16,040
It seems your daughter and Richard are something of an item.

241
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:19,880
That's impossible. He's got a twinkie in the city.

242
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,380
I'm the twinkie.

243
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:25,170
- You're the twinkie?     - She's not a twinkie!

244
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:28,430
Look, this is the best relationship I've been in...

245
00:13:28,640 --> 00:13:31,350
Oh, please! A relationship?

246
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:33,010
Yes, a relationship!

247
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:35,480
For your information, I'm crazy about this man.

248
00:13:35,640 --> 00:13:36,810
Really?

249
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:38,520
Yes.

250
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:42,190
Am I supposed to stand here and listen to this on my birthday?

251
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:47,610
This is a good thing. You said you've never seen Richard happier.

252
00:13:47,780 --> 00:13:48,820
When did I say that?

253
00:13:48,990 --> 00:13:52,620
Upstairs in the bathroom, right before you felt up Mom!

254
00:13:53,620 --> 00:13:56,000
Happy birthday to you

255
00:13:56,210 --> 00:13:59,750
Happy birthday to you

256
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:04,340
Happy birthday, dear Jack

257
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:09,340
Happy birthday to you

258
00:14:10,640 --> 00:14:13,890
It looks so good! Oh, I love it.

259
00:14:14,140 --> 00:14:17,230
I know, so do I! I'm so glad you made me do this.

260
00:14:17,430 --> 00:14:19,310
Okay, let me see yours.

261
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:24,730
Let's see yours again.

262
00:14:25,650 --> 00:14:28,280
We just saw mine. Let me see yours.

263
00:14:31,160 --> 00:14:32,530
Oh, no!

